-- title:
--   Weak approximation for the norm-one group of a rational quaternion algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be non-zero rational numbers and let $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra, with reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\,x_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b\,x_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+ab\,x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$. Let $O\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $O$ is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and $O$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $T$ be a finite set of height-one primes $w$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $s$ assign to each such $w$ an element $s_w\in\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$, where $\mathbb{Q}_w$ denotes the $w$-adic completion. Assume that for every $w\in T$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w\to\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{\mathrm{imI}},z_{\mathrm{imJ}},z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ for all $z\in\mathbb{H}$ and $r\in\mathbb{Q}_w$, one has $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi(s_w))=1$. Let $M$ be a non-zero natural number. Then there is $\gamma\in\mathbb{H}$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\gamma)=1$ such that for every $w\in T$ there exists $z$ in the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ generated by the elements $z_0\otimes c$ with $z_0\in O$ and $c$ in the $w$-adic integers, with $\gamma\otimes 1=s_w+M\cdot z$.
--
--   This is weak approximation for the norm-one group of a quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ at a finite set of finite places: global elements of reduced norm one approximate, to any prescribed congruence level $M$ with respect to the local boxes of an order, given local elements of reduced norm one. It feeds the lemmas that factor a finite idele of the quaternion algebra as a diagonal global element times a local correction, used in the adelic description of quaternionic level structures.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_nrd_eq_one_forall_tmul_eq_add_smul_of_finset.lean

